(GTT-7 Environmental Sensor Datasheet) Tj T*
(Overview) Tj T*
(The GTT-7 measures temperature, relative humidity and barometric pressure) Tj T*
(on a single 3 by 3 millimetre package, and reports all three over I2C or SPI.) Tj T*
(It is designed for battery powered nodes that wake, sample and sleep again,) Tj T*
(so its standby current is held under one microamp across the full range.) Tj T*
(Electrical characteristics) Tj T*
(Supply voltage ranges from 1.71 volts to 3.6 volts. Typical current while) Tj T*
(sampling all three channels at one hertz is 3.4 microamps. The interface) Tj T*
(accepts clock rates up to 3.4 megahertz in I2C high speed mode and up to) Tj T*
(10 megahertz on SPI. Pins tolerate 3.6 volts even when the part is unpowered.) Tj T*
(Measurement accuracy) Tj T*
(Temperature accuracy is plus or minus 0.3 degrees Celsius between 0 and 65) Tj T*
(degrees. Humidity accuracy is plus or minus 2 percent between 20 and 80) Tj T*
(percent relative humidity. Pressure accuracy is plus or minus 0.12 hectopascal,) Tj T*
(equivalent to about one metre of altitude, after the factory calibration.) Tj T*
(Calibration) Tj T*
(Each device is calibrated at the factory and stores its coefficients in) Tj T*
(non-volatile memory. Host software reads the coefficients once at start-up) Tj T*
(and applies the compensation formulas given in the application note.) Tj T*
(Ordering information) Tj T*
(Order code GTT-7-TR ships on tape and reel in quantities of five thousand.) Tj T*
